# PostgreSQL — when to start it

Product uses **`POSTGRES_URL` only**. Do **not** tell the user to start Postgres for pytest or Vitest.

## Do you need a running Postgres?

| Task | Need Postgres? | Why |
| ---- | -------------- | --- |
| `pytest -v` from `backend/` | **No** | Tests use in-memory SQLite; `conftest` stubs `ping_postgres` |
| `npm run test` from `frontend/` | **No** | No database |
| Edit code / read schema | **No** | |
| `alembic upgrade head` | **Yes** | Writes real tables |
| `uvicorn main:app --reload` on the host | **Yes** | Startup `ping_postgres()`; all PG routes |
| Frontend against a real API (`npm run dev`) | **Yes** | API process needs PG |
| pgAdmin / `psql` | **Yes** | |
| `docker compose -f docker-compose.product.yml up` (API + DB) | Compose **starts** Postgres for you | |

There is **no hosted / production Postgres** in this repo yet (P4 ops). “線上” here means **inside Docker / CI**, not a cloud DB.

## Two ways to start Postgres

Both need repo-root **`.env`** (copy from `.env.example`). Never commit `.env`.

### Local (host talks to DB) — most common for `uvicorn` + Alembic

Host must use **`localhost`**, not hostname `postgres`.

```bash
cd ~/assetManager
docker compose -f docker-compose.product.yml up -d postgres
docker compose -f docker-compose.product.yml ps    # must be healthy
```

`.env` must include:

```text
POSTGRES_URL=postgresql+psycopg://<user>:<password>@localhost:<port>/<database>
```

Port is `POSTGRES_PORT` (default `5432`). If WSL already has a system Postgres on 5432, use `5433` (see README §3.D).

Then migrate and run the API on the host:

```bash
cd ~/assetManager/backend
alembic upgrade head
source venv/bin/activate
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

### Compose / “線上” (API and DB in Docker)

Inside the compose network the API uses hostname **`postgres`** (set in `docker-compose.product.yml`). You do **not** set host `POSTGRES_URL` for this path.

```bash
cd ~/assetManager
docker compose -f docker-compose.product.yml up --build -d
docker compose -f docker-compose.product.yml ps
curl http://localhost:8000/ready
```

**GitHub Actions today** (`backend-ci.yml`) runs pytest without Postgres, and `compose-smoke` is the **Mongo** stack on `main`. Product CI + compose postgres is not wired yet.

## Stop

```bash
cd ~/assetManager
docker compose -f docker-compose.product.yml down      # keep data
docker compose -f docker-compose.product.yml down -v  # wipe volume
```

